# SSE lifecycle instrumentation — permanent

Phase 1 SSE lifecycle is **closed**. Do **not** remove or disable this instrumentation when implementing Phase 2a (Redis EventBus) or Phase 2b (Uvicorn SSE).

## Must keep

| Layer | Artifacts |
|-------|-----------|
| BFF | AbortSignal → upstream abort; `bff_sse_proxy_start` / `bff_sse_upstream_connected` / `bff_sse_client_aborted` |
| Django stream | `stream_id`, `X-SSE-Stream-Id`, `sse_stream_opened` / `sse_stream_closed` (+ `close_reason`) |
| Registry + invariant | `register_sse_stream` / `close_sse_stream` / `touch_sse_stream`, `check_sse_invariant`, `sse_invariant_breach` |
| Status + ops | `GET /system/status` → `sse.*` (`invariant_delta`, `active_streams`, …); daily ops CRIT on breach |

## Why

- Redis replaces **in-process fan-out**, not proof that streams close.
- Uvicorn moves **transport**; disconnect/registry/invariant still required on the SSE service.
- Ops diagnose leaks via `stream_id` + `invariant_delta`, not by feel.

## Rules for agents

- Do not gate Phase 2a on a calendar “N consecutive PASS days” window.
- If leak/saturation returns → stop and analyze with the tools above; do not “clean up” by deleting metrics.
- When adding Redis or Uvicorn, **wire** instrumentation into the new path; do not replace it with bus/transport-only logging.
- Reference: [ADR 0005](docs/architecture/adr/0005-gunicorn-sse-worker-evolution.md), [gunicorn-sse-monitoring.md](docs/operations/gunicorn-sse-monitoring.md).
